<title>HONG KONG: China tanker sinks after collision near Hong Kong.</title>
<headline>China tanker sinks after collision near Hong Kong.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Chinese oil tanker caught fire and sank on Thursday after it collided with a Panama-registered vessel in the South China Sea about 36 nautical miles southwest of Hong Kong, the local Marine Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>The eight crew members of the tanker, identified by Lloyds reporting service as the 400 gross tonne Ming Hui, were rescued.</p>
<p>The Panama-registered vessel, Soon Li Fa, was damaged and was proceeding to Kaohsiung, Taiwan, for repairs, Lloyd said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
